# Environment variables

Names only. The Convex dashboard and GitHub Actions secrets are separate stores. A name that appears in both must hold the same value.

Convex injects `CONVEX_SITE_URL`. `convex deploy` injects `VITE_CONVEX_URL` at build time. Do not add those to either secret list.

## Convex dashboard

| Name | Read by |
| --- | --- |
| `AUTH_GITHUB_ID` | Convex Auth |
| `AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET` | Convex Auth |
| `JWKS` | Convex Auth |
| `JWT_PRIVATE_KEY` | Convex Auth |
| `SITE_URL` | Convex Auth |
| `GITHUB_TOKEN` | `convex/actions.ts`, `repoScans.ts`, `repoTags.ts` |
| `CONVEX_BUILD_TOKEN` | `convex/http.ts` |
| `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` | `convex/lib/r2.ts` |
| `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | `convex/lib/r2.ts` |
| `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | `convex/lib/r2.ts` |
| `R2_BUCKET_NAME` | `convex/lib/r2.ts` |

`CONVEX_ENV=dev` makes `dispatchRepoBuild` use workflow ref `develop`. Unset means `main`. Both use `.github/workflows/custom_build.yml`.

`CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` is the Cloudflare account id. `r2.ts` uses it as the R2 S3 endpoint host.

## GitHub Actions secrets

| Name | Workflow |
| --- | --- |
| `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` | `custom_build.yml` |
| `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | `deploy.yml` |
| `CONVEX_BUILD_TOKEN` | `custom_build.yml` |
| `CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY` | `deploy.yml` |
| `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID` | `custom_build.yml` |
| `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | `custom_build.yml` |
| `R2_BUCKET_NAME` | `custom_build.yml` |

Shared with Convex, same value: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`, `CONVEX_BUILD_TOKEN`, `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `R2_BUCKET_NAME`.

## When adding a variable

Add the name here in the same change as the code that reads it.
